---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, LAST_UPDATED, SITE_NAMES } from '../../data/site-config';
import { route } from '../../i18n/routes';
const lang = 'en';
---
<PageLayout title={`Cookies – ${SITE_NAMES[lang]}`} description="This Austrian pay calculator sets no cookie and stores nothing about you. Site stability is checked anonymously with Microsoft Clarity in its cookie-free mode." lang={lang} noindex={true} breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Cookies' }]} showAuthor={false}>
  <div class="prose prose-slate max-w-none">
    <h1>Cookies</h1>
    <p>Supplement to the <a href={route('privacy', lang)}>privacy policy</a>.</p>
    <h2>No cookies</h2><p>The site sets no cookie on any page, and the calculators store nothing on your device: salary, children and commuting distance stay in the open page and are gone once you close it. That is also why there is no cookie banner: there is nothing to agree to.</p>
    <h2>Anonymous stability checks</h2><p>To catch broken pages, script errors, slow loading and buttons that do nothing, the site loads Microsoft Clarity in cookie-free mode. Clarity then sets no cookie (no <code>_clck</code>, <code>_clsk</code>, <code>MUID</code> or <code>CLID</code>), gives each page view its own one-off identifier and does not link your visits. Page content and inputs are masked before anything is sent.</p>
    <h2>Blocking it anyway</h2><p>If you would rather not be measured at all, block the clarity.ms domain or use a content blocker; the calculators work exactly the same.</p>
    <p>Questions: <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>. Last updated: {LAST_UPDATED}.</p>
  </div>
</PageLayout>
